WLAN: the Wi-Fi controller an IOEthernetController under the wlan node, its address there as local-mac-address (HackiOS 80f5042).

MobileGestalt asks for the Wi-Fi address of every bundle lsd registers. It reads local-mac-address
from the device tree's "wlan" node first, and otherwise waits up to 5 s per question for a service
of the class IONetworkController under that node. With neither, a first boot that rebuilds
LaunchServices in full takes hours, SpringBoard waiting (the ios-sapphire port found this first).
Publish the controller as an IONetworkController -> IOEthernetController -> IO80211Controller --
SystemConfiguration calls en0 Wi-Fi by that ancestry -- and put the address on the node. When the
platform publishes the node as a nub (HackiOS) the controller goes under the node; on spes the node
is under arm-io and the platform expert makes nubs for the top level only, so the address goes on
the device tree entry itself (the property MobileGestalt reads first) and the controller stays
under the platform.

